# RadialPilot v15 referenced layout studies

Unapproved. Built-in image_gen. Actual Unreal source path verified; reference is packed texture R channel displayed as opaque grayscale. Three new layout concepts. Not imported. These are shading images, not independent alpha masks. Review limitation: some contour bands from reference remain and need correction before final authoring. Live level rendering was not captured.

## A

Use attached image as the EXACT cloud painting STYLE AND GRAYSCALE VALUE reference, not layout. It is extracted shading channel of RadialPilot_v15. Create a NEW square polar UV cloud layout with this same subtle fluffy painted detail, rich white center-facing crowns, smooth medium gray density bodies and darker outward bases. Match reference shading range and scale hierarchy, no blue tint, no flat posterized planes, no leaf/lens shapes, no tiny repetitive cauliflower stamping. Ignore technical thin dark/white contour artifacts in reference, do NOT reproduce outlines. Black sky background; outward cloud bases gradually softly dissolve into black for this shading concept. Center zenith remains completely clear within radius 0.55 of circular layout radius. Concentrate clouds in outer 0.65–0.98 radius, thick large cloud banks interspersed with small distant banks. All crowned tops face center, especially northwest small clouds crowns southeast, northeast southwest, north down, east left, south up, west right. Bases face outward. Long axes flow tangent to local circle, no spiral no radial tails. Varied shallow silhouette lobes and broad density masses, fine shading concentrated around crowns matching reference. Outer distant clouds same paint style but lower contrast, readable bases. Circle fits square with black corners and small margin. No labels. Four unequal separated outer cloud groups, balanced but irregular spacing, medium-size banks and small distant banks between, clear angular sky gaps, avoid fourfold symmetry.

